From: TITAN-NT <titan@localhost>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 17:00:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] server, ntdll: Enable fsync on Android without shm_open or
 futex_waitv.

fsync was switched off on Android because Bionic has no POSIX shared memory
and the app seccomp filter traps futex_waitv (449). Both are fixable without
changing the protocol.

The shared memory becomes a file in the config directory, which both sides
already agree on and which is the same MAP_SHARED mapping that futexes are
keyed by, so cross-process wakes still work. shm index 0 is never handed out
to an object, so it carries a wake epoch: signallers store the object, bump
the epoch and wake it, and waiters sleep on the epoch with FUTEX_WAIT_BITSET
instead of futex_waitv. A waiter reads the epoch before scanning the objects,
so a signal between the scan and the wait makes the wait fail with EAGAIN
instead of being lost. Waking every waiter on every signal costs more than
futex_waitv did, but it keeps NtWait* out of wineserver.

Amphora-Origin: replaces ca552f7c9c, which only turned fsync off
Amphora-Upstream: android-only
---
diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/fsync.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/fsync.c
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/fsync.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/fsync.c
@@ -63,22 +63,26 @@
